Cell[TextData[{
 "MGroups is a mathematica package that implements a part of finite group \
theory. It offers a user-friendly interface for performing a range of \
computations involving finite groups including ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["Z", "n"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "2ede3b73-bc28-e84f-a483-c2c3c98b42ae"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["U", "n"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "97233a46-9f7b-cb41-bd1d-f9f79759cab4"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["D", "n"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "7c266199-8f9b-4a4c-8951-6498d9baec52"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["S", "n"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "d84cfb14-7bf0-a849-88e5-3c3072db26f3"],
 ", and more. The package allows users to define and analyse groups through \
Cayley tables and provides functionality for investigating group operations, \
subgroup structures (lattices), group morphisms, and more.\n Each group is \
defined in terms of its Cayley table representation itself, and operations \
are applied appropriately."
}], "Text",
 TaggingRules->{},
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9578542221525726`*^9, 3.9578543107358265`*^9}, {
   3.9578543445024014`*^9, 3.9578543673132343`*^9}, 3.95785835036747*^9},
 CellTags->"DefaultContent",
 CellID->441612482,ExpressionUUID->"dd4c3208-a8f0-7c4c-b316-839df03eb997"],

Cell["\<\
Computational tools play a vital role in modern mathematics by automating \
complex and often tedious calculations, thereby freeing users from manual \
labour and enabling deeper exploration of abstract concepts. In that essence, \
MGroups is designed primarily for undergraduate students beginning with group \
theory, as well as for educators seeking a user-friendly tool to demonstrate \
group-theoretic concepts interactively.\
\>", "Text",
 TaggingRules->{},
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9578543828952217`*^9, 3.9578543987335167`*^9}},
 CellID->475399438,ExpressionUUID->"67e60a40-2459-e948-840f-24c4fc57d821"]
}, Open  ]],

